job_description:
Venture , a public listed company in SGX, is a leading global provider of technology services, products and solutions with established capabilities spanning marketing research, design, research and development. Over the years, Venture has built know-how and intellectual property with expertise in several technology domains.

These include life science & genomics, molecular diagnostics, medical devices and equipment, healthcare and wellness technology, lifestyle consumer technology, health improvement products, instrumentation, test and measurement technology, networking and communications, fintech, as well as computing, printing and imaging technology.

Headquartered in Singapore, the Group comprises over 30 companies with global clusters in Southeast Asia, Northeast Asia, America and Europe, and employs over 12,000 people globally.

At Venture, our people are our most valuable asset. We are committed to unifying culture, encouraging innovation, and harnessing the collective strengths and synergies of our human capital to deliver compelling differentiation, advancing Venture’s position as a leading global provider of technology solutions, products and services.

We’re looking to add a
Senior System Analyst, IT (BI)
in
Singapore
. The position is based in our
HQ
at
Ang Mo Kio
.

As a Senior System Analyst, IT (BI), you will:

• In charge of managing and implementing end-to-end BI solutions, from requirements gathering to deployment and maintenance using waterfall Project Management methodology for Group Wide stakeholders;

• Managing and implementing digital initiatives that emphasizes flexibility, collaboration and feedback using agile approach for Group Wide stakeholders;

• Understand and analyze users’ business requirements and processes, study ROI, and recommend solutions proposals to management;

• Collaborate with BI and cross-functional team members on projects that can achieve the company’s goals;

• Design and develop scalable, efficient, and optimized data models, ETL processes, and data visualizations for efficient delivery to Power BI;

• Evaluate, select, and implement appropriate Azure services and tools to meet business requirements and optimize solution performance;

• Provide technical guidance and mentorship to junior team members;

• Manage projects and support activities with team members;

• Make proposals that encompass, but are not limited to architecture diagrams, data flow diagrams, system specifications, requirements, and user manuals for the organization;

• Supervise best practices and standards in BI solution development via code review;

• Ensuring data integrity, accuracy, and security with effective governance for sensitive information protection;

• Participate in evaluating emerging AI/ML technologies such as Generative AI through studies and proof of concepts.

What skills and experiences are we looking:

• Degree/Diploma in Computer Science, Information Systems, Computer Engineering or equivalent, with min 5 years relevant experience.

• Manufacturing experience and supply chain knowledge is preferred;

• Strong hands-on experience in designing data models, ETL processes, and data visualizations using AWS S3, Glu, Redshift, Lake Formation, Azure Data Factory, Databricks,
Azure Data Lake Storage
, and Power BI;

• Solid understanding of
data warehousing
and data integration concepts as well as
data governance
and security;

• Experience in project activities;

• Experience in ETL and data analysis by using
Python
such as
pyspark
, pandas, scipy, numpy;

• Experience in
GenAI
project execution will be advantageous;

• Basic understanding of SAP ERP modules will be advantageous.

• Translate business needs into high-level technical specifications and design using Azure and Power BI;

If you embody the spirit of excellence, passion for discovery, innovation and enterprise, and the desire to make a difference in the world of technology and electronics, come join the Venture team!
Be Part of the Global Venture Family.
Disclaimer:

By submitting your application to Venture Corporation Limited and its group of companies, you acknowledge and agree that any personal data you provide will be processed for the purpose of evaluating your application for employment.
If you are not selected for this position, we may retain your personal data to consider you for future employment opportunities unless you inform us otherwise. Should you wish to withdraw your consent or request access to or correction of your personal data, plea

